{"kind": "journal", "text": "Findings: dominant structure is a persistent cross-sectional risk premium: long high long-window vol (std 120 best, 0.97 alone) plus short high short-window kurtosis (kurt 20-60 all near 0.85 alone). Combined at roughly equal weight the family plateaus at SR 1.28-1.35 across kurt windows 15-60, z vs rank transforms, weightings, smoothing, even a sign-binarized version - strong evidence the effect is broad and parameterization-insensitive. Delay tests: SR holds through 10d delay (spike to 1.6 at exactly 10d treated as train noise, not exploited) and halves by 20d, so the signal is a slow characteristic and should transfer OOS. ts_z versions confirm it is the level, not innovation, that is priced. LT reversal, skew, beta, corrm, maxr are weaker overlapping expressions of the same complex and dilute the core. Final picks: three diverse members of the plateau (z-based kurt 20+40, rank-based kurt 20+60, wide 4-window kurt ensemble at 1:2 vol:kurt) rather than the single train-max, to hedge estimation noise.", "ts": "2026-09-01T06:32:26.763423+00:00"}
{"kind": "report", "top3_chosen": ["add(cs_z(std(120)), add(neg(cs_z(kurt(20))), neg(cs_z(kurt(40)))))", "add(cs_rank(std(120)), add(cs_rank(neg(kurt(20))), cs_rank(neg(kurt(60)))))", "add(add(cs_z(std(120)), cs_z(std(120))), add(add(neg(cs_z(kurt(15))), neg(cs_z(kurt(20)))), add(neg(cs_z(kurt(40))), neg(cs_z(kurt(60))))))"], "chosen_sr_train": [1.3266, 1.3461, 1.3379], "rationale": "Core alpha: long high 120d volatility, short high short-window kurtosis. Each leg is strong alone (std 120 SR 0.97; neg kurt 20-60 SR 0.83-0.85) and the combo plateaus at SR 1.28-1.35 across kurt windows 15-60, z vs rank normalization, weight choices, smoothing and delays up to 10d - a broad, parameterization-insensitive, persistent level effect rather than a tuned spike. The three picks are diverse plateau members (z with kurt 20+40; rank with kurt 20+60; 1:2 weighted wide 4-window kurt ensemble) to hedge estimation noise instead of maximizing train SR.", "n_batches_used": 7, "ts": "2026-09-01T06:32:34.365556+00:00"}
